\begin{abstract}
\noindent This report synthesizes observational diagnostics across five field and synthetic regimes (CASES-99, FLOSS, BLLAST, SHEBA, and GABLS3) with Morlet Continuous Wavelet Transform (CWT) flux filtering, weak-form equation discovery (WSINDy), and Geometric Singular Perturbation Theory (GSPT) slow-manifold diagnostics. We evaluate a $2 \times 2$ factorial validation architecture to separate vertical discretization bias ($\Delta z$) from internal gravity wave contamination ($e_{\text{wave}}$), using $p$-FEM Gegenbauer spectral expansions and stiff Galerkin solvers.
\end{abstract}

\begin{tcolorbox}[executivebox]
\textbf{Executive Takeaways \& Benchmark Highlights:}
\begin{itemize}\setlength{\itemsep}{2pt}
    \item \textbf{Data Ingestion \& Wavelet QC:} Processed high-frequency time series and profile data, applying CWT dynamic scale-gap extraction to isolate true turbulent flux ($Co_{w\theta}$) from wave orbital variance ($e_{\text{wave}}$).
    \item \textbf{Factorial $2 \times 2$ Framework:} Systematically isolates observation operator discretization artifacts ($\mathcal{H}_{\text{SHEBA}}$) from wave contamination to test the existence of the critical fold locus ($C_{\text{fold}}$).
    \item \textbf{Equation Discovery \& Galerkin Solvers:} Discovered non-linear candidate closures evaluated via Pareto frontiers ($RSS$ vs. $R^2$), Leave-One-Site-Out (LOSO) cross-validation, and stiff \texttt{Rodas5P} integration.
\end{itemize}
\end{tcolorbox}

