\section{Theoretical & GSPT Validation Architecture}
% ==============================================================================

Horizontal momentum evolution within the planetary boundary layer is governed by the turbulent flux divergence equation:
\begin{equation}
    \frac{\partial u}{\partial t} = f(v - v_g) + \frac{\partial}{\partial z} \left( K_m(z, Ri_g) \frac{\partial u}{\partial z} \right)
\end{equation}

To disentangle observational artifacts from genuine dynamical bifurcations on the critical manifold $\mathcal{S}_0 = \{(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}) \mid \mathbf{f}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}; 0) = \mathbf{0}\}$, we execute a $2 \times 2$ factorial experiment comparing raw vs. flux-filtered signals across continuous fine-grid $p$-FEM SCM solutions and discrete 5-level sensor operators ($\mathcal{H}_{\text{SHEBA}}$).

